--- !u!114 &1000000000000000003
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 3783339790580182791}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2e9f1291c0e34c0292b645cf45aa79eb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Pages:
  - '<b>Seeing Differently</b>


    These pages describe what people have told researchers
    about living with the conditions in this room.


    The summaries are shortened.'
  - "<b>Central Vision Loss</b>\n\n\"I am having trouble reading even the biggest
    letters\" \n\nSome people can no longer rely on recognising faces, even of relatives.
    Some stop going to gatherings because they can't tell who is there."
  - '<b>Dyslexia</b>


    Dyslexia is a reading difference. In interviews, adults
    describe the strain of writing and proofreading at work.


    Colleagues sometimes
    take their mistakes for laziness.'
  - "<b>Colour Blindness</b>\n\nFor some people, red can look brown, dull or even
    black, and pale colours can be hard to tell from grey. \n\nEveryday tasks can
    be affected too, such as judging if food is cooked or fruit is ripe."
  - '<b>Light Sensitivity</b>


    In people with achromatopsia, glare is described
    as one of the most debilitating symptoms.


    Filter glasses can help, and
    children are advised to sit away from the window.'
  - '<b>Visual Snow</b>


    Adults with visual snow syndrome describe effects on
    sleep, mental health, daily routines and comfort in light.


    About a third
    also name something positive about it.'
  m_FontSize: 0.16
  m_TextThickness: 0.3
  m_PaperMaterial: {fileID: 2100000, guid: a01f9507321d4c758540c495a322648c, type: 2}
  m_TextColor: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1}
  m_FlipDuration: 0.6
  m_ReturnWhenReleased: 1
  m_ReturnDuration: 0.4
